# XCU val
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.val.001
anchor     utilities/val.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/val.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       val on an intact SCCS file writes nothing and exits 0.
test       t/001-valid-file.sh

assertion  XCU.val.002
anchor     utilities/val.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/val.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -r of an existing SID passes, a nonexistent SID sets 0x04, and an
           ambiguous or invalid SID sets 0x08.
test       t/002-sid-check.sh

assertion  XCU.val.003
anchor     utilities/val.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/val.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A -m name that is not the module name sets 0x01 and a -y type
           that is not the type flag sets 0x02, matching values give 0.
test       t/003-module-and-type.sh

assertion  XCU.val.004
anchor     utilities/val.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/val.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/val.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A file that is not SCCS sets 0x10, no file operand sets 0x80, an
           unknown option sets 0x40, messages start with the pathname and -s
           silences them.
test       t/004-bad-input.sh

assertion  XCU.val.005
anchor     utilities/val.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Over several files the status is the OR of the individual codes.
test       t/005-aggregate.sh

assertion  XCU.val.006
anchor     utilities/val.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/val.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With the - operand each input line is a command line, and a
           discrepancy is reported as the input line, an empty line and an
           indented pathname message.
test       t/006-stdin-lines.sh

assertion  XCU.val.007
anchor     utilities/val.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       A modified SCCS file sets the corrupted-file bit 0x20 in the exit
           status of val.
test       t/007-corrupted.sh
